### Secrets / local config ###
*.env
application-local.yml
# `src/main/resources/application.yml` is NO LONGER ignored, and must not be again.
#
# Ignoring it meant it was never in the repo, so the Docker image built from this repo shipped with
# no configuration file at all: on Railway every `ember.*` property was missing and the app died at
# startup binding JwtProperties. The committed file is placeholders only — every value reads an
# environment variable, and no secret has a real default.
#
# Real local values live in `backend/config/application.yml` instead (ignored below). Spring Boot
# loads `./config/application.yml` automatically, at higher precedence than the one on the
# classpath, so local development picks it up with no profile or run-configuration change.
# Leading slash matters: it anchors this to `backend/config/` only. Unanchored, `config/` matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth — including `src/main/kotlin/com/ember/backend/config/`, which
# would silently stop any newly added SecurityConfig-style class from ever being committed.
/config/
*firebase*.json
*service-account*.json
